==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|zele}}, from {{der|en|fro|zel}}, from {{der|en|LL.|zēlus}}, from {{der|en|grc|ζῆλος||zeal, jealousy}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*yeh₂-|t=to search}}. Related to {{m|en|jealous}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ziːl/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/zil/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-zeal.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːl|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[fervour]] or [[tireless]] [[devotion]] for a person, cause, or ideal and determination in its furtherance; [[diligent]] [[enthusiasm]]; [[powerful]] [[interest]].
#: {{syn|en|ardour|eagerness|enthusiasm|intensity|passion}}
#: {{ant|en|apathy}}
#: {{ux|en|She extols the virtues of veganism with missionary '''zeal'''.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Romans|10|2|url=https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Romans+10&version=KJV|passage=I bear them record that they have a '''zeal''' of God, but not according to knowledge.}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Hind and Panther|part=3|page=96|url=http://name.umdl.umich.edu/A36627.0001.001|passage='''Zeal''', the blind conductor of the will}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1779|author=w:David Hume|title=w:Dialogues Concerning Natural Religion|volume_plain=part 12|page=143–144|url=http://name.umdl.umich.edu/004895521.0001.000|passage={{...}} the highest '''zeal'''  in religion and the deepest hypocrisy, so far from being inconsistent, are often or commonly united in the same individual character.}}
#* {{RQ:Austen Emma|volume=1|chapter=14|page=250|passage=[He] would begin admiring her drawings with so much '''zeal''' and so little knowledge as seemed terribly like a would-be lover,}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1962|author=w:Rachel Carson|title=w:Silent Spring|location=Boston|publisher=Houghton Mifflin|chapter=15|page=248|url=https://www.fadedpage.com/books/20151002/html.php|passage=The stockman’s '''zeal''' for eliminating the coyote has resulted in plagues of field mice, which the coyote formerly controlled.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A person who [[exhibit]]s such fervour or tireless devotion.
#: {{syn|en|zealot}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1614|author=w:Ben Jonson|title={{w|Bartholomew Fair (play)|Bartholomew Fair}}|location=London|publisher=Robert Allot|section=act v, scene 5|page=85|url=http://name.umdl.umich.edu/A04633.0001.001|passage={{...}} like a malicious purblinde '''zeale''' as thou art!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1642|author=w:Thomas Browne|title=w:Religio Medici|location=London|publisher=Andrew Crooke|page=5|url=http://name.umdl.umich.edu/A29868.0001.001|passage={{...}} there are questionlesse both in Greeke, Roman and Africa Churches, solemnities, and ceremonies, whereof the wiser '''zeales''' doe make a Christian use, and stand condemned by us;}}
# {{n-g|The [[collective noun]] for a group of [[zebra]]s.}}
#: {{syn|en|dazzle|herd}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Zeal of Zebras: Animal Groups on an African Safari|author=Alex Kuskowski|year=2012|page=8|ISBN=1614802807|passage=A '''zeal''' of zebras confuses predators. Each zebra has a different set of stripes.}}

